---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="Studio BDY Ltd is the company of Lee Brady, a programme director and delivery manager based in Bath with more than 25 years of delivery in telecoms, pharma and the public sector."
  current="about"
>
  <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 48px">
    <div class="container two-col" style="align-items: center">
      <div class="stack gap-m">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1 style="font-size: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 56px)">Studio BDY delivers.</h1>
        <p class="lead">A one-person company with a long track record, engaged where an experienced hand is needed: programmes that have to land, and small businesses that want the useful parts of AI.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center">
        <img class="headshot" style="width: 240px; height: 240px" src="/images/lee-brady.jpg" width="640" height="640" alt="Lee Brady" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 40px">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Lee Brady</h2>
      <p>Lee is a programme director and delivery manager based in Bath. Since 2021 he has been programme director, through Studio BDY, on the delivery of a new capability for one of the UK's leading mobile operators. Before that: senior programme and engagement roles with technology and consulting firms, and twelve years as a consulting director delivering transformation programmes for major UK telecoms operators, from governance and PMO leadership to third-party and vendor management and the production running of a national inventory platform.</p>
      <p>Earlier still, five years on site with mobile operators across Europe as a technical account manager and project manager, and a start as an engineer. He holds a BEng (Hons) in Aeronautical Engineering from the University of Bath.</p>
      <p>Alongside the programme work, Studio BDY takes on freelance Excel and automation projects for clients in many industries and several countries, and builds bespoke iPhone and iPad apps. The Excel habit goes back a long way: the KPI tooling for that national inventory platform was Excel VBA, written to make the performance of a whole solution stack visible to the people who had to fix it.</p>

      <h2>How Studio BDY works</h2>
      <p>Directly. Engagements are with Lee, not a bench. The first conversation is about where you are and what done looks like; the scope, cadence and governance are agreed up front; then the work is hands-on and embedded with your team, remote or on site in the UK.</p>
      <p>Sectors for programme delivery: telecoms, pharma and the public sector. Excel and small-business work has been for clients across many industries, delivered remotely to several countries.</p>
      <p>On AI: Studio BDY uses it every day to run its own admin, and brings that experience to small businesses. The rule is the same everywhere it is applied: the tools draft, monitor and prepare; a person decides and sends.</p>

      <h2>What clients say</h2>
      <blockquote class="quote" style="margin: 0">
        <p>“Lee is a truly great professional. As a client of Lee's, I was always impressed with how he went above and beyond to solve problems and see deliveries to the end. Lee is a considered problem solver and he always creates options that are helpful and well thought through. I wouldn't hesitate in recommending Lee.”</p>
        <cite>Philip Black, CEO and Co-founder, Cormirus · client</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <blockquote class="quote" style="margin: 0">
        <p>“Lee was an instrumental member of the team in the business development and customer engagement leading to the sale and then took ownership of the complex delivery program within a challenging environment. Lee's positive attitude, depth of knowledge and calm demeanour were significant in generating customer confidence to undertake the program and complimentary to his outstanding leadership of a multi-geography agile delivery team.”</p>
        <cite>Mark Harris MBA, senior leader on a Tier 1 telecoms transformation programme</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <p class="small muted">Both quoted from recommendations on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lee-brady/" rel="me noopener">Lee's LinkedIn profile</a>.</p>

      <h2>The company</h2>
      <p>Studio BDY Ltd is registered in England and Wales, company number 13538439, VAT registration GB389 2525 56. Registered office: 38 Dollar Street, Cirencester, GL7 2AN. Lee works from Bath.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="panel-cta row">
        <div class="stack gap-s">
          <h2 style="font-size: 30px">Get in touch</h2>
          <p class="muted">Email is best. Lee replies to every message himself.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a href="mailto:lee@studiobdy.com" class="btn btn-primary">Email lee@studiobdy.com</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lee-brady/" rel="me noopener" class="btn btn-secondary">LinkedIn ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
